.TH ACCEPT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
accept \- accept a pending connection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.B int accept(int descriptor, struct sockaddr* address, socklen_t* length);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Accepts a pending connection and returns a new descriptor.
When address is non\-NULL, length supplies the address buffer capacity and
receives the actual peer address length. Pass NULL for both to omit the peer
address. The listening descriptor remains open.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the new descriptor, or \-1 with errno set.
Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR listen (3crunch),
.BR accept (2)
